WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:09.330
PRESENTER: Historically, wheels
were made of metal or wood.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:11.610
With the invention of
air-filled car tires

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.650
in the early part
of the 20th Century,

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.200
the ride was revolutionized.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.110
The inflated rubber tires
could better absorb the bumps

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:21.330
on the road, and the
addition of tread

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.070
gave the invention
serious traction.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.625
Car tires have come a long
way in the last century.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.740
The modern summer tire
is made of 10 to 15

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.870
different components
which include

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:39.230
natural and synthetic
rubber, chemical additives,

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:40.910
and carbon black, a pigment.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.080
Giant blenders mix these
ingredients under heat

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.240
and tremendous pressure.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.790
There are various formulations
for different parts

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:50.810
of the tire.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:54.080
In each case, the result
is gummy rubber dough

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.590
which machinery then rolls
into sheets to wait further

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.230
kneading and processing.

00:01:00.230 --> 00:01:04.550
Polyester fabric unrolls into
a machine called a calender.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:07.850
The calender is equipped with
rollers that apply warm rubber

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.155
to both sides of the fabric.

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:12.470
This produces a rubberized
fabric that will

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:14.300
be used to reinforce the tire.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.850
This fabric ply is kneaded
because rubber alone isn't

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:20.245
sturdy enough to make a tire.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:26.590
Numerous cotton cords now spin
off bobbins simultaneously.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:30.350
Machinery pulls them onto
the warm rubberized fabric.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.375
They land on a bit of
an angle and adhere.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.150
This cording creates
channels that

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:40.580
provide pathways for venting
air during the actual tire

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:41.380
building.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.280
Making rubber for
tread requires three

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.650
different rubber formulations.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.410
Extruders shape the
three streams of rubber,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:54.130
and then they enter a die
that forms them into one.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.400
Many paint rollers apply
different colored stripes.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:59.560
It's a coding system
for identification

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.530
of the ingredients
during processing.

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:06.700
To avoid tension, the system
creates slack in the feed.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.520
A blade slices the
tread rubber to length.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.930
Next, many steel cables uncoil
at once to make the bead--

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.970
the part of the tire that
gives it the strength it

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.710
needs to stay on the wheel rim.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:23.230
Machinery arranges the cables
in the desired configuration

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:25.750
and encases them in rubber.

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.780
More equipment rolls the
bead material into hoops

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.400
sized to fit the wheel rim.

00:02:35.130 --> 00:02:37.440
They're now ready
to build the tire.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.650
Using a special rotating
drum, a worker arranges

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.120
the two bead hoops on it.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.840
Next up is an airtight
piece of rubber

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.915
that will act as an inner tube
followed by the corded ply.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:53.130
Inflated bladders roll
the rubber around the bead

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.320
on both sides and then retract.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.950
A surfer applies side
walls to the beads.

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.655
Little rollers fold the
side walls over the beads.

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:07.805
This completes the inner
part or skeleton of the tire.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.770
They assemble the
outer layer separately,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:14.425
beginning with strips of rubber
embedded with steel cord.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.070
The system wraps
this rubber around

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:19.630
a second tire-building drum.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.610
Next up are narrow
strips of rubber ply.

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.740
The computerized
system winds them

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.850
with just the right amount of
tension for a graduated effect.

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:34.210
They're now ready for the
last layer, the tread rubber.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.895
Machinery applies it to the ply.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:42.250
It's time for the two tire
fabrications to become one.

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.620
A transfer ring
collects the assembly

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.600
and transfers it
to the inner part.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:51.090
Compressed air inflates
the tire to shape it,

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.145
and all the sticky
layers adhere together.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.520
The machine rolls the
edge of the tread rubber

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.585
over the side walls.

00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:05.310
They now have what's known in
the industry as a green tire,

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.590
an uncured tire
without tread pattern.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:13.635
Next, it's into a mold to
bake and shape the tire.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.010
The two parts of the mold come
together like a waffle iron.

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:23.910
Inside, hot steamy bladders
expand to shape the tire

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.430
and transfer the
tread pattern to it.

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:29.335
This specific tread pattern
is designed for summer tires.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.530
This cutout of a car tire
demonstrates how all the layers

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:35.505
have been fused together.

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:39.360
The time in the hot
pressurized mold

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.930
has caused the rubber to
vulcanize, a chemical reaction

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:46.350
that transforms it from a weak
and sticky substance to one

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.570
that's strong and elastic.

00:04:48.570 --> 00:04:51.310
A worker trims excess rubber.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.300
After final inspections
confirm the tire's shape is

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.640
uniform and
geometrically correct,

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.110
the tire is ready for shipment.

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:02.480
It's time for the
rubber to hit the road.

